      "text": "greene lab The Greene Developmental Cognitive Neuroscience Laboratory seeks to understand how cortical and subcortical brain systems develop, become individualized, and interact to support cognitive, motor, and sensory functions in typical and atypical development, with a particular focus on Tourette syndrome. We use multimodal cognitive neuroscience approaches, including functional and structural MRI, functional connectivity, EEG, and behavioral measures, to study the organization and development of brain networks at both the group and individual levels. Donate to the Greene Lab lab members research publications participate data/software directions wiki contact join us",
